  "trigger": "Actual registered operator /datapack enable/disable/reordering -> resource reload and world configuration setter -> level.dat save -> dedicated startup lightweight LEVEL-versioned configuration restore -> selected resource load -> real crafting result lookup and feature check.",
  "input": "World-authored ordered Enabled IDs and Disabled veto list, enabled_features names, old retired minecraft:update_1_20 flag/removed_features memory, actual currently discoverable vanilla/world/mod packs plus required packs and feature requests.",
  "output": "Main.loadOrCreateConfig uses stored configuration when nonnull, initMode false; missing configuration falls back dedicated initial pack selection with initMode true. LevelStorageSource lightweight scan excludes Player/WorldGenSettings, runs LEVEL DFU and readDataConfig current typed codec. FeatureFlagRemoveFix at3440 removes update_1_20 from enabled_features and appends name to removed_features; current PrimaryLevelData retains and reserializes removed string set. Actual PackConfig/configurePackRepository discovers packs, adds Forge mod packs to enabled list, checks present enabled packs, disabled policy, auto-add source and requested-feature subset, forces vanilla if selection empty, then required packs may be inserted by repository. Selected pack resources form MultiPackResourceManager, JSON recipes scan selected resources, actual RecipeManager replaces available recipes. Server CraftingMenu queries live server manager, assembles matching recipe then gates ItemStack result by world feature flags; valid result enters actual result slot and sync packet. World data setter/write retains selected IDs/current complement disabled and joined known flags for next startup. Whole world content activation contract1, each flag/pack/recipe/DFU/helper0.",
  "preservation": "Distinct whole49 remains world geometry seed/generator/dimension reconciliation and future terrain consumer. This is operator-authored active content catalogue and experimental capability selection controlling which recipe/function/loot/tag sources are loaded, independently mutable via /datapack without changing stored seed or dimension definitions. Whole survival policy2d98 remains difficulty/lock/hardcore, not content activation. Shared WorldLoader/LevelSettings/PrimaryLevelData/save wrappers0; old update_1_20 removal supports same whole content capability contract, not a second migration item. No accepted owner narrowed and no new client assets/building credit.",
  "limits": [
    "Static nativeForge1.20.1-47.4.10 pinned local sources only. Actual source jar SHA verified; listed34 native/Forge files line content ZIP normalized compared (actual computed count in metadata). No DFU/game/Java execution, network, userworld, current Dynasty validation, production/checklist/ledger/Git changes.",
    "readDataConfig resultOrPartial can use partial parsed known data; if no result returns DEFAULT, not old file fallback. readLevelData only tries level.dat_old when loader null; getDataConfiguration catches exceptions and returnsnull, unlike full getLevelData path which can throw. Bad codec may normalize todefault while seeming valid, no opaque unknownpack/feature custody guarantee.",
    "FeatureFlagRegistry codec produces error with partial known set for unknown IDs, unknown names dropped on rewrite. FeatureFlagRemoveFix moves specifically update_1_20 into removed_features at version3440; existing removed list retained then Primary parse collects onlystrings intoSet, dedup/noorder, writerretains. No general arbitraryfeature backward compatibility; all historical LEVEL fixes not audited. Supplied wrong DataVersion can bypass/misapply.",
    "Missing previously Enabled pack onlywarns and is omitted from selected; getSelectedPacks saves actualselected plus currentlyavailable-unselected disabled, so missing enabled/disabled IDs can disappear after save. Missingpack returning later can autoenable according source rather than originalintent; not tombstone. Existing Enabled wins even if also Disabled because initialset includesit and disabled prevents later checks, notremoves. Required repository packs inserted after validation can reappear despite intended disable or flags; no strict disabled veto forrequiredpacks.",
    "Forge configure mutates DataPackConfig.DEFAULT and loaded config enabled list via addModPacks. Safe mode loads Forge modpacks plus vanilla and DEFAULT_FLAGS, despite Main log onlyvanilla. ResourcePackLoader/Finder implementations not fully read; ForgeHooks accessor checked and canthrow if called beforeloaded. No claim modpack hidden/required behavior exactbeyond repositoryshown.",
    "Existing-world PackConfig uses initial enabled flags asalloweduniverse and joins them back after currentpackrequestedflags, so removingpack doesnot necessarilyrevoke feature flags. Newworld initMode temporarilyallowsallknownfeatures but finalactualrequestedfeatures. Not per-player earnedskills/paymentauthorization, no dynamic content download.",
    "PackRepository getSelectedIds returns ImmutableSet overselected list; exactduplicate behavior and iteration order delegatedGuava, no arbitrary platformorderproof. Available discovered by TreeMap ID, sameIDlater sourcereplaces. Required insertion and defaultPosition can change effectivepriority. Full Pack.Position, FolderRepositorySource, fallback perfileoverride/filterinternals not deepread; selected namespace resourcechain concrete but no claim arbitrary duplicate recipe precedence verified.",
    "Reload command sends success before async completion and catches futurefailure tofailuremessage; not durableACK. MinecraftServer.reloadResources loads newresource managers before setSelected/worldData setter, but closesold/swapsnew then mutatesothercomponents without rollback; exception during post-load install canleave partialstate. Reload request list may includemissing IDs: resourceopen filtersnull, repositoryset removesmissing after. Requiredpacks inserted by setSelected afterresourcesalreadyopened can temporarilydisagree with loadedmanager. Worldconfig change saves later, no immediate fsync, player saveAll doesnotprove worldmetadata flush.",
    "Current fulllevel read receives reconciled configuration fromWorldLoader, not re-reading rawstoredconfiguration intosettings. Shared49 generation still receives currentdatapackregistry and canoverride saved matchingdimension; that wholeterrainlimitation retained. Data pack content selection can change bothrecipes/terrain, but this credit onlyactivation policy notgeneratoragain.",
    "RecipeManager skips underscored/failedconditions/nullserializer/badJSON entries and replaces maps; failedrecipe isnotretainedopaque. Actual hadErrors flag remainsfalse inshownmethod, not a trustworthy failurecounter. Full serializers/Forgeconditions notdeepread; actual result CraftingMenu check uses same live manager and Level flags. No gameplayearnedunlock owner added (existing recipebook/advancement retained).",
    "BUNDLE specialcurrentnative source iscreative-tabvisibility check, NOT claim actualBundle item requiredflag: actual Items.BUNDLE no requiredFeatures initializerobserved; generic ItemStack/FeatureElement gate source exists but no fabricated bundlecraftingrestriction. Creative tab clientpacketfeature propagation notdeepread. Itemrequired defaultVANILLA andworldflag omission canaffectgeneric gate; no concretecurrentcustomitem runtimeproof.",
    "Primary writer merges configuration encodeleft, logsencoderight andcouldomit config. Currentremoved_features stringsretained separately fromactiveflagdecode. createTag andForgehook outside saveDataTag try maythrow; compressedtmpwrite/safeReplace caught/logged, no callerACK/fsync/worldatomicproof.",
    "Alllistedboundedranges actuallyread; initialSimpleJsonimports5-11 andPack80-98 truncations repaired in separateoutputs. Fullclasses onlywherecompleteextentlisted; not wholeMinecraftServer/LevelStorageSource/Primary/Item/CreativeTab. Originalindexcandidate/method/AST checked acrossallserializedstatuses/no-family; no collision. Referenceowner1 pendingmainreview, not TODOcomplete orproductiongate met."
